detaileddescription.para:
For path points R_i, segment i stores six doubles:

columns 0..2: d_i = R_(i+1) - R_i;

column 3: d_i dot d_i;

column 4: l_i = |d_i|;

column 5: S_i = sum_(j<i) l_j, the arc length at the segment start. The squared length, rather than its reciprocal, retains the original division in the closest-point calculation. A short single-work-item geometry kernel accumulates S_i in increasing segment order; zero-length segments contribute zero length and remain excluded from the nearest-segment search.
